**Decision:** I reject the report, park the executor, merge and deploy nothing, and send the operator one poll. The redo and the review are not ordered until they answer.

## 1. Check the tab and the claim — Bash, foreground (read-only)

```bash
herdr agent get rdp-lang     # need "focused": false, agent_status idle|done
herdr agent read rdp-lang --source recent-unwrapped --lines 400 > "$ORCH_INBOX/rdp-lang.last"
grep -nF 'superpowers:' "$ORCH_INBOX/rdp-lang.last"
grep -nE 'ansible-playbook|ssh |changed=' "$ORCH_INBOX/rdp-lang.last"
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-lang rev-parse HEAD
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-lang status --short
```

The output goes into the backlog entry. It does not change the rejection, because the report itself carries no artifacts.

## 2. Reject and park — Write, then Bash, background

Write `$SCRATCH/reject-rdp-lang.txt`:

```
REJECTED — rdp-lang, report at 4ba90e0 (branch feat/rdp-lang).

The brief required superpowers:writing-plans, superpowers:test-driven-development and
superpowers:verification-before-completion, and the artifact each produced. The report
names no skill and carries no artifact: no plan path, no failing-test-first output, no
verification command output. "Idempotent re-run: changed=0" has no command output, and
executors have no host access in this project.

Nothing is merged or deployed until the gates are met.

Park now: no commits, no push, no PR, no host connection, no rework. Wait for my next message.
Reply in English, one line: PARKED — branch, head SHA, working tree clean yes/no.
```

```bash
# run_in_background: true
herdr agent prompt rdp-lang "$(cat "$SCRATCH/reject-rdp-lang.txt")" --wait --timeout 300000; \
herdr agent read rdp-lang --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$ORCH_INBOX/rdp-lang.last"
```

