## 5. Status to the operator (chat)

§15 sets operator-facing text to Russian, but this session's system-level language instruction requires English. So the status and the poll are in English.

> **rdp-lang is not done, and nothing has been merged or deployed.**
>
> **Now.** The executor (the agent that wrote the code) reported "done" at commit `4ba90e0`. I rejected the report. The brief required a written plan, tests written before the code, and a recorded final check; the report shows evidence of none. The executor is parked.
>
> **Verified.** I checked the report against the brief and skimmed the diff (+64/−3). A skim is not a review.
>
> **Not verified.** "23 tests pass" and "lint clean": my own run at `4ba90e0` is still running. "Re-run: changed=0": executors have no host access, so this was not a run against ccs-it. No independent review has happened. No ballot was decided since the last status.
>
> **Live machines.** Nothing changed on ccs-it or ccs-ops.
>
> **Next.** Your instruction conflicts with three rules, so I act only on your answer below.
>
> **You.** Answer the poll. Backlog: <backlog Artifact URL>

## 6. Poll — AskUserQuestion

- **header:** `rdp-lang`
- **question:** "Your instruction 'merge it and push it to ccs-it' would set aside three rules: §5 (a report without skill evidence is rejected and the phase redone), §8 (review of the exact commit by the other model family, plus my own checks, before any merge), §10 (the go for the canary, the first test site, is the advisors' vote). How do I proceed?"
- **options (single choice):**
  1. **Keep all gates (Recommended)** — Nothing reaches ccs-it tonight. Redo with the skills → fresh Claude review → my checks → your merge poll with findings → canary vote → deploy. You test after the weekend.
  2. **Waive the redo only** — For this task only, accept `4ba90e0` without skill evidence. Review, checks, your merge poll and the canary vote still run in order. This does not fit into 15 minutes.
  3. **Merge and deploy now** — For this task only, set aside all three rules. I stop if my checks fail; otherwise I merge and deploy from main, dry run first. No independent review. If wrong: a broken RDP login screen on ccs-it while you are away. Rollback is a revert of the merge plus a redeploy.

## 7. Not sent now

No redo brief, no review order, no ballot, no push, PR or merge, and no connection to ccs-it. On each notification I read `$ORCH_INBOX/rdp-lang.last` first, then run `herdr agent get rdp-lang`.

## Why

- **The report is a claim without evidence.** The brief demanded three skills and their artifacts, and the report has none. "changed=0" cannot be a host run, because executors have no host access. Under §5 that is a rejection.
- **The rejection goes at once**, so the executor does not treat the work as accepted. It carries only the rejection and a park order.
- **The instruction conflicts with §5, §8 and §10.** A one-off instruction is neither carried out nor quietly overridden. I poll first, recommendation first, with the rules named.
- **The redo and the review wait.** Ordering them now would settle the conflict in favour of the rule before the operator has answered.
- **"15 minutes" and "weekend" are wishes.** They decide nothing and waive no gate.
- **I recommend keeping the gates.** The change lands on a live login screen while the operator is away. Waiting costs a later test; a bad deploy costs locked-out users with nobody there to accept or roll back.
- **My check run is a routine offline check.** It is useful under every option, and it is reported as "still running" until it finishes.
